{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Elohim, return na</b> — now, like: הן נא זקנתי or אוי נא לנו. And the general rule, thus is the explanation of every נא in Scripture, and it is in Arabic. The opposite: אין does not fall upon standing tense. And because he mentioned צבאות, he said: מן השמים." "And the meaning of זאת — that זאת is itself the vine that you brought up from Egypt."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 80, :notes {0 "The phrase הפוך אין נופל על זמן עומד is opaque; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:37.051759822Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}